meta {
  name: Vendor Lookup
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/vpas/vendor-lookup?identifier={{vendorUpiId}}
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Resolves a vendor's UPI ID (or mobile number) to a VPA row a vendor payout can target
  (`VPAService.getVPAForVendorPayout`). An unknown UPI ID is looked up at the bank and saved as a
  driver-less VPA with a mapping to the caller's torg. A UPI ID that is verified and linked to a
  driver of the same torg is refused. Not open to DRIVER.

  Response (staging 2026-10-06; staging's mock lookup names every UPI ID "Test User"):

  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Success",
    "statusCode": 200,
    "data": { "id": 401, "name": "Test User", ... }
  }

  Use `data.id` as `vpaId` in `payment-gateway/vendor-payout`.
}
